# ── THE vLLM version line — ONE home, two readers ────────────────────────────
#
# Readers:
#   • tooling/src/stack/vllm-setup.sh  — sources this file and installs $VLLM_PIN into the bare-metal venv.
#   • tooling/src/stack/lib/engines-compose.ts — reads $VLLM_VERSION for the engine containers' image tag
#     (`vllm/vllm-openai:v$VLLM_VERSION`) in the generated docker/compose.engines.yaml.
# Before this file the two were a hand-copied pair, which is how the retired sibling compose profile rotted.
#
# VLLM_PIN is the venv's install spec and is DERIVED from VLLM_VERSION (`vllm>=<major>.<minor>,<next minor>`).
# It is written out rather than computed so the shell stays a plain `source`; the derivation is re-computed
# and compared in tests/tooling/stack/lib/engines-compose.test.ts, so the two lines cannot drift.
#
# BUMPING IT DOES NOT TOUCH A LIVE VENV. `engines.sh` runs `vllm-setup.sh` only when the venv binary is
# MISSING, so an existing install keeps running the version it has until the owner runs
# `bash tooling/src/stack/vllm-setup.sh` by hand (or deletes the venv): the pin marker then mismatches and
# the venv is rebuilt FROM SCRATCH (several GB). The container arm needs no such step — the image tag
# changes with this file and `docker compose pull` fetches it.
VLLM_VERSION=0.29.0
VLLM_PIN="vllm>=0.29,<0.30"
